pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% The one-knob control: `pbc.pbp` with the `proofgoal 1` / `qed;` wrapper removed and nothing
% else changed. The subproof now owes what it always owed -- a contradiction from `~C` -- and
% `rup >= 1 ;` cannot supply it, so the UNFIXED checker refuses this too. That is what pins the
% forgery to the FABRICATED GOAL rather than to "`pbc` subproofs accept anything".
f 1 ;
pbc >= 1 : subproof
rup >= 1 ;
qed;
output NONE;
conclusion UNSAT ;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
